**Diagnosis:** Your Python 3.13 installation had a broken pip — the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory existed in site-packages, but the actual `pip/` source code package was missing. The pip entry point scripts (`pip`, `pip3`) were present and tried to import `pip._internal.cli.main`, which failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.

**Fix:** Removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which properly installed the full pip package (both source and metadata).

